WEBVTT

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.230
Meriella and Donatella are mean.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.250
I know that I'm the one 
who forgot to check

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.270
if all the doors were locked,

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.050
but they still could have come with me.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:18.410
Who's there?

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.540
Is someone there?

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.850
Show yourself, intruder!

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.270
A ghost in the kitchen?

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:45.930
How ridiculous.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.190
I'm sure she was just tired 
and was seeing things.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.980
But Isabella is saying she saw one.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.440
She said she had long hair and 
was wearing a white dress.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.880
She only thought she saw 
it because she was scared.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.940
If she would regularly train her mental state

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.580
so little things wouldn't scare her...

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.040
So you say, but you're 
actually scared, aren't you?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.340
What did you say?!

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.010
It's not showing up.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.690
Shut up.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.730
What's the matter?!

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.960
Oh, uh, it's nothing...

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.880
It's a misunderstanding!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.260
I didn't mean...

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.510
Wh-White?

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.760
I-I'm sorry! I didn't mean to look!

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.420
Ow!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.820
A Pace repellent?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.620
Yes. I didn't mean to scare everyone.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.830
So this is the ghost's identity.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.060
How ridiculous.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:53.920
I wanted it to look real, 
so I also used some alchemy.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.110
I didn't expect you to be so surprised.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.280
So why the repellent for Pace?

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.840
I guess I can figure that out on my own.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.140
Yes.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.850
I still haven't overcome 
the fear I felt that day...

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.170
<i>Give them to me...</i>

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.280
<i>Who is it?</i>

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.060
<i>Dolce...</i>

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.640
<i>Dolce...</i>

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.130
<i>Pace?</i>

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.790
<i>I want to eat...</i>

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.580
<i>Give them to me...</i>

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.170
<i>Dolce...</i>

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.480
So a sleepwalking Pace ate all of them?

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.080
It's no laughing matter!

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.980
Thanks to him, I was awake all night.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.170
So, I set up that trap so he 
can't bother me this time.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.870
If that's the case, 
you should have told us prior.

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.310
How troublesome, for crying out loud.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:47.910
But, Luca,

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.180
what are you going to do with 
all these sweets you've made?

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.370
I'm taking them to the piccolino.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:53.930
Piccolino?

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:57.590
Oh, you hadn't been informed yet, Milady?

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:03.150
The piccolino is an event for little 
children that the family holds.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.290
We invite all the kids from 
Regalo and entertain them.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.910
We put on shows and play calcio.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.680
It's a lot of fun!

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.120
I know!

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.810
You should come, too! 
It's the day after tomorrow.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:15.580
You will, won't you?

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.190
You're going, too, right, Nova?

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.960
He skips out every time.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.590
I'm busy.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.840
So you say.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.140
But the truth is you're so short, 
you can't handle kids, huh?

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.970
So, Princess, it'll be 
the day after tomorrow.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:30.800
Okay.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.070
Hurry up! It's going to start!

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.310
Wait for me!

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:40.230
Come on! If you don't hurry, 
I'm leaving you behind!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.720
I'm sorry.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.330
Are you hurt?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.120
I haven't seen you before.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.050
Do you live around here?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:55.310
Are you going to the piccolino, too?

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.710
Piccolino?

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.250
And now if I can have 
everyone's attention.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.420
What I'm about to show you is the 
most secretive of secret techniques!

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.010
A dove will appear.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.090
Wow!

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.090
Uh... Huh?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.390
Time to change players.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.900
No one's impressed with 
doves anymore, Luca.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.990
What?!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.280
Let's try something different, shall we?

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.770
Having fun is all about 
excitement and thrills.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.710
Do you want to hear a scary story?

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.670
All right! Debito's awesome!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.330
No, that's scary!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.650
Actually, the scary moon demon, Diavolo,

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:50.310
lives here on Regalo.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.190
It all happened one stormy night.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:07:00.970
An orphaned child came to this 
church in search of help.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:05.360
It was there, that the child met Diavolo.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:11.500
But the child, of course, 
didn't realize it was demon.

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:14.920
How unfortunate.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.950
The child's soul was severed in two.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.290
One half became the 
demon's minion, Belzebù,

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.000
who resides in the darkness, hiding.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:30.260
What about the other half?

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.610
The other half wasn't able 
to go to Heaven or Hell.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:38.970
It's said that the ghost 
still haunts this church,

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:43.240
looking for someone to play with.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.360
Speaking of which, it's right over there!

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.020
Hey, now, don't freak out too much.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.030
Fukulota, your timing was 
more than impeccable.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.380
Apparently, that was a little too intense.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.090
Hey, now, don't look so sad.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.300
You'll ruin your beautiful face.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.050
So Debito likes children.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.450
How unexpected.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:20.100
Despite how scary he looks, 
he's good at taking care of others.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:21.750
Indeed.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.320
He was always nicer to the younger kids.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.090
Have you two known Debito for a while?

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:31.860
Yeah, the three of us grew up together.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:35.070
We often played in this church, too.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.070
How nostalgic.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.300
<i>You can't hide the sound of 
your stomach growling, Pace.</i>

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.260
<i>Man.</i>

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.090
<i>Where's Debito?</i>

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.630
<i>I still haven't found him.</i>

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.150
<i>If there's one thing he's 
good at, it's hiding.</i>

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.030
<i>Pace.</i>

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.810
<i>Hey! We found Debito!</i>

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.620
The look on Debito's face as he was

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.280
sleeping then was like an angel.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.690
I'm still the angel of love even now.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.170
Isn't that right, Bambina?

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:35.310
When did he become such a terrible adult?

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.250
What?

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:39.050
You want to tell me exactly 
what's so terrible about me?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.680
Now, now, adults don't fight.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.650
Luca, please!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.530
Thank you for the food!

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.850
Those idiots are on the 
same level as kids.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:02.570
The dessert for today 
is baci di dama, Milady.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:05.220
It means "kiss from a lady."

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:06.730
It looks delicious!

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:09.030
Kiss from a lady, eh?

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.460
I'd say a kiss from 
Bambina is much sweeter.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.200
Debito, step away from her!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.050
And stop trying to seduce Milady!

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.890
Seduce? This is just a greeting.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:26.470
Your greetings are improper!

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.460
And you call yourself a man of Regalo?

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:31.440
You're too rigid, you stuffed shirt!

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:34.310
You're not a kid, so shut your mouth.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.990
Now then, since we're done eating,

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.280
I guess it's time for this.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.620
Yay, calcio!

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:47.410
Out of the way!

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.530
Why the hell are you being so serious

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.090
playing against children?

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:54.750
So naïve!

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.330
You better stop him, Libertá!

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:00.340
Got it!

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:02.640
Do you think you can stop me?

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:07.680
They call me Regalo's mangostano!

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:08.930
Milady—

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.100
Whoops.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.100
You hit the jackpot, I mean Luca.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:19.020
Are you trying to kill me, Pace?!

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.240
Sorry, sorry.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.840
What do you mean, "sorry"?!

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:25.480
What if that shot had hit 
Milady or the children?!

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:28.410
Not to mention the piccolino is an 
event to entertain the children!

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.120
Your entertainment comes after that!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.190
You okay, Princess?

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:32.920
Yes.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.170
The wind...

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:39.910
What about the wind?

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:41.830
Oh, it's nothing.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:42.830
Hey!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.670
Let's hurry up and continue the game!

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.280
Yeah, I'll be right there!

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:00.510
How stupid.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:05.320
May I come in?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.420
Mama.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:15.710
I came here to scold you today.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.760
You didn't go to the piccolino again.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.510
I have work to do.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.850
I don't know how

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.300
to interact with the children.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:39.310
To think of nothing and 
just have fun with them.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.930
It's easier said than done for me.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:45.850
Nova.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:01.450
It's no good, it's just getting worse.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.380
We should probably hurry.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.320
Are you all ready?

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:09.100
Yeah.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.220
We'll split up the kids

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.130
into groups depending 
on where they live

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:13.810
and see that they get home safe.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:17.460
Princess and Libertá, 
watch over the remaining.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.190
Okay.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.150
Leave it to us.

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:26.820
Now then,

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:29.830
what should we do until Debito 
and the others return?

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:34.920
Don't look so scared!

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.290
You're children of Regalo!

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.880
Storms shouldn't bother you!

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.370
I know!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.470
You should go to them.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:53.970
You're worried about the children 
at the church, aren't you?

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.270
It's written all over your face.

00:13:57.260 --> 00:14:00.980
The three higher-ups, Luca, and 
that idiot are all with them.

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.450
I'm not worried...

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.070
You're so kind.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:07.990
Nova,

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.870
kindness is nothing to be ashamed of.

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:14.040
It is a form of weakness.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.090
You're wrong.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:28.180
To be kind, to be weak, 
they both hold great power.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.510
But you have confined 
that within a hard armor.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:37.830
However, we are the reason that happened.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.260
Mama, let's not talk about that...

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:43.740
The responsibility that I

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:47.790
and Mondo have for taking away 
your childhood is rather heavy.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:52.370
However, let me say this 
despite knowing that.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.990
As long as you wear that armor,

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:59.380
you won't be able to grow any more.

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.300
You should relax more, Nova.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:07.920
Stop being scared of hurting 
others or being hurt yourself.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:13.260
That may be the hardest thing for you.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:18.630
But I want you to enjoy your life.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.850
The way your heart desires...

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:36.830
Good grief. There he goes.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:42.680
Storms are excellent, 
especially spring storms.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:45.750
It makes you feel like 
something is about to begin.

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:47.640
The weather was clear!

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.380
The ship that carried the hero, Libertá,

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.880
along with a mountain of cargo,

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.930
headed north on the Aegean Sea.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.470
However, soon after that, black clouds

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.660
started to form and the ship was quickly

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.560
engulfed by a storm!

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.140
We're doomed, Dante!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.850
All hands on deck! Hurry!

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.270
Aye!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.820
What are you doing, Libertá?

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.280
Hurry up and come down!

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.750
Stay there, I'll be right...

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:16.790
Dante!

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.580
And then?

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:23.250
What happened next?

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.330
Oh, uh...

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.210
What did happen...

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.920
Was the captain okay?

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.910
Oh, yeah, Dante...

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.340
er... the captain was fine,

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:37.710
thanks to the hero.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.010
How did the captain survive?

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.810
What did the hero do?

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:43.140
Um...

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:44.760
Libertá?

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.050
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:50.020
I'm not too smart, so I forgot.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:51.150
What?

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:52.470
Sorry about that.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:57.440
Damn it, it's just getting worse.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.040
This should be all of them.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.040
You two head back to the mansion.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:03.970
Okay.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:06.550
I'm leaving it up to you to 
escort Bambina back safely.

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:07.680
Got it!

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:14.310
All right.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:16.880
Checking complete.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.230
Let's go home, Princess.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:19.100
Okay.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.150
But, you know, it really 
seems like a ghost could—

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:32.380
Nova!

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:34.830
What the hell are you doing here?

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:35.650
Where are the children?

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:39.590
Oh, Debito and the others 
got them all home safely.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:41.660
I see.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.850
We're about to head back, too.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.460
Do you want to—

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.300
So all of the children have gone home?

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.140
Huh? Yeah.

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:52.940
Then, what is that?

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:54.930
Huh?

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.050
What's your name?

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:00.550
Elmo.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.510
Where do you live, Elmo?

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.430
We'll take you home.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.330
You seem rather thin,

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:10.810
and your face is pale.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:14.400
Really? I think you worry too much, Nova.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:15.860
But...

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:20.990
U-Um, I wanted to ask her something.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:22.530
Me?

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.460
I've been feeling a little weird.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.970
My chest started thumping all of a sudden.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.480
Do you know what's wrong with me?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:34.880
What is this feeling?

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.880
Am I sick?

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:39.700
You don't seem to have a fever.

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:42.550
Actually, you're freezing cold!

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:44.540
It'd be bad if he caught a cold.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.550
Go find something to warm him up.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.630
There was a blanket in the basement.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:49.400
I'll go get it.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:52.400
Hey, miss,

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.950
this is the first time 
I've ever felt like this.

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:09.930
Why am I thinking about that now?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.630
Sorry about the wait!

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:23.620
It hit nearby.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.470
Huh? Elmo?

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.600
I'm going home now.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:31.660
What do you mean, you're going home?

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.650
Hang on a sec, we'll take you home.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:35.140
I'll go.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.590
Thank you, mister.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.240
But I'll be fine on my own.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.410
Don't be stupid. It's storming outside!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:43.990
Goodbye.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:47.450
Hey!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.590
He disappeared.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.140
By some weird coincidence,

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:01.970
he wouldn't happen to be 
the ghost of the church

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.490
that Debito mentioned, would he?

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.420
Welcome home.

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:16.490
Did you have fun today?

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:51.970
We will now begin our 
repentance for the day.

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:52.760
Yes.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:56.290
Choose the one that should be 
punished, by naming their card.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.740
La Forza.

00:21:57.740 --> 00:21:58.920
L'Eremita.

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:03.280
Tonight's sinner is you, L'Eremita!

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.300
What? Why is it me?

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:08.220
Your use of language at the church,

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.790
what in the world was that?!

00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:11.930
What if the children were to copy you?

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:16.060
So, we're going to have you drink this.

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:18.150
Whatever it is, it stinks.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:21.460
This is a magical tea 
which, in a single sip,

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:24.950
would make a ruffian speak 
properly and beautifully.

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:26.960
Resistance is absolutely futile!

00:22:26.960 --> 00:22:28.910
Whatever. All I have to 
do is drink it, right?

00:22:39.310 --> 00:22:41.540
Oh, whatever is the matter, you two?

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:42.460
What?!

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:46.100
Oh, what a wonderful feeling.

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:48.980
It feels as though my body 
and soul are being cleansed.

00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:50.790
just by speaking properly.

00:22:51.310 --> 00:22:52.600
I thank you, Luca.

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:55.070
Y-You're welcome...

00:22:55.070 --> 00:22:56.730
This isn't good.

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:59.060
This is too disturbing.

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:01.120
Hey, this isn't Debito!

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:02.560
Hurry and change him back!

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:04.960
That won't be possible until 
the medicine wears off.

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:06.490
What?! When will that be?!

00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:09.580
Whatever is the matter, Pace?

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:11.320
Have you taken ill?

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:12.720
No, uh...

00:23:12.720 --> 00:23:13.860
That simply won't do.

00:23:13.860 --> 00:23:15.110
Have you consumed too much again?

00:23:15.670 --> 00:23:17.660
Allow me to rub your back for you.

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:18.930
N-No!

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:21.090
Don't come any closer!

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:22.840
Now, don't be like that.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.700
S-Stop! S-Stop!

00:23:30.790 --> 00:23:34.410
Hey there, signorina.  
Is this your first time in Regalo?

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:37.120
How about I show you around?

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:39.480
Come on, come a little closer...
